{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.62,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "polarity",
      "components": ["D1"],
      "pins": ["D1.1", "D1.2"],
      "nets": ["+5V", "J8.2/J4.2/C6.1/C2.1/C4.1/C3.1 (servo power rail)"],
      "observed": "The PMEG3030EP Schottky D1 is drawn with its cathode (bar side) tied to the +5V rail and its anode tied to the servo power rail (the node feeding J8 pin 2, J4 pin 2 and the C6/C2/C4/C3 100 µF bank). This is the opposite orientation to the correctly-drawn series input diode D2 (SS54), whose cathode sits on the +5V side so that current flows from the external jack into +5V.",
      "expected": "Per the spec, this diode must conduct FROM +5V INTO the servo rail: 'From +5V, a second diode D2 (PMEG3030EP ...) feeds a dedicated servo power rail backed by four 100 µF capacitors (C1–C4) before reaching J3/J8 pin 2.' The anode should be on the +5V side and the cathode on the servo-rail side.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "From +5V, a second diode D2 (PMEG3030EP, annotated \"3A 360mV\" in the schematic — a low-forward-voltage-drop Schottky) feeds a dedicated servo power rail backed by four 100 µF capacitors (C1–C4) before reaching J3/J8 pin 2."},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "D1 PMEG3030EP 3A 360mV — cathode bar at the +5V node, anode at the J8.2/J4.2/C6/C2/C4/C3 servo-rail node (sheet m5-pantilt.kicad_sch, page 1, region B/C column 4)."}
      ],
      "impact": "With the diode reversed, +5V cannot forward-bias into the servo rail, so the bulk-capacitor bank and the servo headers' power pin (pin 2) are never energized from the board's 5V supply. Servos would receive no power (and the rail could instead back-feed +5V through D1), defeating the inrush-buffering function the spec describes.",
      "confidence": 0.62
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The build's reference designators are renumbered versus the spec but the circuit topology, component types and values otherwise match; the one deviation the drawing supports is that the servo-rail Schottky D1 (PMEG3030EP) is installed in reverse (cathode on +5V, anode on the servo rail), which would prevent the servo power rail from being fed from +5V."
}

